<section class="retreat-section retreat-intro">
  <div class="retreat-section__inner">
    <p>For ten years we've gathered online and on conference stages to ask one question together: what does it mean to follow Christ into the future? This fall, for the first time, we're taking that question into the woods. A retreat, not a conference — less presenting, more presence.</p>
    <p>We'll come to embody the thing we keep pointing at — a hopeful, rational, future-facing faith.</p>
    <p>We work against illness, hunger, oppression, injustice, and death — and once a year, it's good to do that work shoulder to shoulder, in person, with people who see what you see.</p>
    <p class="retreat-theme-line">The theme that will hold our weekend: <strong>the shape of progress is the face of Christ.</strong> Come find out what we mean.</p>
  </div>
</section>

